                <pb facs="0218" n="116" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg116"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/88: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Curtis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-08T15:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">January 8,
                                1919, 3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            January 9</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">?</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >12.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>The President informs me that Honduras is building road and telegraph line in
                    Nicaraguan territory which has never been claimed by Honduras, and that he has
                    ordered local governor to arrest the workmen, taking care that he do so in the
                    territory undisputably Nicaraguan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
